{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++17 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++17 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing ll = long long;\nconstexpr int MAXN = 510;\n\nint MOD;\n\nint add(int a, int b) {\n    return (a += b) >= MOD ? a - MOD : a;\n}\n\nint mul(int a, int b) {\n    return (ll)a * b % MOD;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    \n    int n, m;\n    cin >> n >> m >> MOD;\n    \n    int C[MAXN][MAXN] = {};\n    for (int i = 0; i <= n; ++i) {\n        C[i][0] = 1;\n        for (int j = 0; j < i; ++j) {\n            C[i][j+1] = add(C[i-1][j], C[i-1][j+1]);\n        }\n    }\n    \n    int f[MAXN] = {}, g[MAXN] = {};\n    f[0] = 1;\n    g[0] = 0;\n    \n    for (int i = 1; i <= m; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 1; j <= i; ++j) {\n            int comb = C[i-1][j-1];\n            int term = mul(mul(comb, i+1), mul(f[j-1], f[i-j]));\n            f[i] = add(f[i], term);\n            \n            int part1 = mul(mul(comb, i+1), add(mul(f[j-1], g[i-j]), mul(g[j-1], f[i-j])));\n            int part2 = mul(mul(comb, (j-1)*j/2 + (i-j+1)*(i-j)/2), mul(f[j-1], f[i-j]));\n            g[i] = add(g[i], add(part1, part2));\n        }\n    }\n    \n    ++n;\n    int dp[MAXN][MAXN] = {};\n    int dp2[MAXN][MAXN] = {};\n    dp[0][0] = 1;\n    dp2[0][0] = 0;\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j <= m; ++j) {\n            if (!dp[i][j]) continue;\n            for (int k = 0; j + k <= m && i + k + 1 <= n; ++k) {\n                int coef = mul(mul(dp[i][j], f[k]), C[j+k][j]);\n                dp[i+k+1][j+k] = add(dp[i+k+1][j+k], coef);\n                \n                int inner = add(mul(dp2[i][j], f[k]), mul(dp[i][j], g[k]));\n                int val = mul(C[j+k][j], inner);\n                dp2[i+k+1][j+k] = add(dp2[i+k+1][j+k], val);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    \n    cout << dp2[n][m] << '\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\ndef main():\n    input = sys.stdin.readline\n    MOD = 0\n    \n    n, m, MOD = map(int, input().split())\n    \n    MAXN = 510\n    \n    # Initialize combination table\n    C = [[0] * MAXN for _ in range(MAXN)]\n    for i in range(MAXN):\n        C[i][0] = 1\n        for j in range(i):\n            C[i][j+1] = (C[i-1][j] + C[i-1][j+1]) % MOD\n    \n    # Initialize f and g arrays\n    f = [0] * MAXN\n    g = [0] * MAXN\n    f[0] = 1\n    g[0] = 0\n    \n    for i in range(1, m + 1):\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            comb = C[i-1][j-1]\n            term = (comb * (i + 1) % MOD) * (f[j-1] * f[i-j] % MOD) % MOD\n            f[i] = (f[i] + term) % MOD\n            \n            part1 = (comb * (i + 1) % MOD) * ((f[j-1] * g[i-j] % MOD + g[j-1] * f[i-j] % MOD) % MOD) % MOD\n            part2 = (comb * ((j-1)*j//2 + (i-j+1)*(i-j)//2) % MOD) * (f[j-1] * f[i-j] % MOD) % MOD\n            g[i] = (g[i] + part1 + part2) % MOD\n    \n    n += 1\n    dp = [[0] * MAXN for _ in range(MAXN)]\n    dp2 = [[0] * MAXN for _ in range(MAXN)]\n    dp[0][0] = 1\n    dp2[0][0] = 0\n    \n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(m + 1):\n            if dp[i][j] == 0:\n                continue\n            for k in range(m - j + 1):\n                if i + k + 1 > n:\n                    break\n                coef = (dp[i][j] * f[k] % MOD) * C[j+k][j] % MOD\n                dp[i+k+1][j+k] = (dp[i+k+1][j+k] + coef) % MOD\n                \n                inner = (dp2[i][j] * f[k] % MOD + dp[i][j] * g[k] % MOD) % MOD\n                val = C[j+k][j] * inner % MOD\n                dp2[i+k+1][j+k] = (dp2[i+k+1][j+k] + val) % MOD\n    \n    print(dp2[n][m])\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00014447122521232814, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.128175288438797, -0.00011848701251437888, -0.00524098752066493, -0.02159416675567627, -0.013499756343662739, -4.184158387943171e-05, -9.536738616588991e-07, -0.7983625531196594, -0.007607062812894583, -1.07287787614041e-05, -3.576272320060525e-06, -0.31560051441192627, -0.009806079789996147, -9.30981186684221e-05, -0.02548905462026596, -0.0005279577453620732, -0.4954531490802765, -0.0205435361713171, -0.460646390914917, -3.4570634852570947e-06, -0.06898538768291473, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.00012420836719684303, -0.00019000156316906214, -0.00037746457383036613, -2.825220326485578e-05, -3.814689989667386e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -7.152555099310121e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.009765943512320518, -4.458328112377785e-05, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -9.536738616588991e-07, -0.00908396765589714, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.0005696581210941076, 0.0, -1.311301275563892e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.2519361674785614, -2.5987286790041253e-05, -0.39440953731536865, -0.11356590688228607, -0.656602144241333, -0.013809142634272575, -0.12693004310131073, -6.794906312279636e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.3841830625315197e-06, -2.205347482